making sure no one can take the app and publish it, in whole or in part, as their
own product.

1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   1.1  View, read, and study the source code in this repository.
   1.2  Fork or clone the repository for personal, educational, or non-public use
        (e.g. running a local debug build on your own device for testing).
   1.3  Modify the source code and build it locally for your own private use.
   1.4  Submit Pull Requests to this repository with bug fixes, features, or
        improvements, subject to Section 3.
   1.5  Reference or quote short excerpts of the code (e.g. in a blog post, talk,
        or Stack Overflow answer) with attribution back to this repository.

2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

